## Summary of the ordered request path
1. Security filter chain — default: permit all (`DisableSecurityConfig`); if enabled: HTTP Basic auth required + `@PreAuthorize(ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN)`.
2. Jackson deserializes JSON body into `OwnerFieldsDto`.
3. `@Valid`/`@Validated` runs Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone — `@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size`). On failure → `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400.
4. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` runs: `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (id & pets ignored).
5. `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (`@Transactional`) → `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (Spring Data JPA `persist`). No uniqueness checks, side-effects, events, or encoding.
6. On flush, Hibernate validates the `Owner` entity constraints (notably stricter `telephone` rules); DB assigns the identity `id`. A DB constraint violation → `handleDataIntegrityViolationException` → 404.
7. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, `Location` header set, `201 CREATED` returned.

No `@PrePersist`/JPA listeners on `Owner`; the only custom `@Constraint` in the repo (`PetAgeValidation`) does not apply to owners.
